										<P>
											<span id="dl_news__ctl0_Label1"><font face="Verdana" color="White" size="1"><P align=left>This is an automatic news entry posted by GuildWizard.  After you read it, you can delete it by logging in as and administrator and clicking the Add/Edit/Delete News link<BR><BR>Steps to configuring your site:<BR><BR>1) Change your colors/textures by logging in with your Administrator account and click on the Color Configuration button<BR>2) Add your members by clicking the Add Player button. Your member's default password will be their username until they change the password.<BR>3) Configure your roster to show the columns you want by clicking the link on the roster <BR>4) Configure your member's profile page to show the information you want by clicking the link on the profile page<BR>5) Add your news by clicking the link on the Main page<BR>6) Create any custom pages, perhaps your guild's Charter, or maybe an Ally List, by clicking the Custom Page Maker.  Be sure to make note of the link it generates so you can create a button for the page!<BR><BR>Remember, GuildWizard.com is still working out the bugs!  If you encounter a problem, PLEASE email me at sharbel@guildwizard.com with a description of the problem.  You can use the same email address for suggestions or features you would like to see added.<BR><BR>I am working on making the documentation for the various features.  The best way to learn how to use the features, is by using them.  If you are stuck, feel free to email me and I will explain how to do the various tasks.  Again, this will be a non-issue when I get around to the documentation.<BR><BR>Lastly, you can keep track of recent additions/changes/fixes by visiting www.GuildWizard.com   I update the news section on the main page regularily with my recent progress.<BR><BR>Thanks for using GuildWizard.com!<BR><BR>Sharbel<BR>www.GuildWizard.com<BR></P></font></span></P>
